{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfNCsH9j3CCzgTr5gfVSm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```json\n[\n  {\n    \"unitKey\": \"q02\",\n    \"questionNumber\": 2,\n    \"part\": null,\n    \"status\": \"PASS\",\n    \"textIssues\": [],\n    \"choiceIssues\": [],\n    \"answerIssues\": [],\n    \"explanationIssues\": [],\n    \"figureIssues\": [],\n    \"sourceIssues\": [],\n    \"verifiedEvidence\": [\n      \"The stem matches the attached original figure (問2, printed page -2-, footer T2−H 005, consistent with reviewedFromPage [5]) word for word, except that the original's full-width comma「，」is written as「、」. The meaning is unchanged.\",\n      \"All five options (1)–(5) match the original in wording and numbers: 250 kW, 3 kW, 250 kW / 50 kW, and 200 V. The units kW and V are correct.\",\n      \"The official answer is (3), which matches the manifest-fixed answer {question:2, part:null, answer:'3'}. The candidate's officialAnswer is also '3'. No change was made.\",\n      \"Law Article 2(2) (effective 2024-04-01) removes demand facilities with maximum demand of 500 kW or more from 自家用電気工作物 as the law uses the term. A 250 kW facility is therefore in scope. This supports the reasoning for (1), (3) and (5).\",\n      \"Law Article 3(1) says only a first-class electrician (第一種電気工事士) may work on 自家用電気工作物. It removes Paragraph 3 work (特殊電気工事) from that rule. This matches the explanation's claims that (1) is permitted and that (3) falls outside Paragraph 1.\",\n      \"Law Article 3(2) lets both first-class and second-class electricians (第一種・第二種電気工事士) work on 一般用電気工作物等, and sets no output limit. This matches (2), where the option itself says the equipment is installed in a 一般用電気工作物, and (4). It also supports the note in the (2) explanation that the second-class license has no separate output cap.\",\n      \"Law Article 3(3) and Enforcement Regulation Article 2-2(1)(ii) make work on the generator and related parts of an 非常用予備発電装置 a 特殊電気工事. That work requires a 特種電気工事資格者 certificate, and the regulation sets no output condition. A first-class license alone is not enough, so (3) is the incorrect statement. This matches the answer and explanation.\",\n      \"Enforcement Regulation Article 2-2(1)(i) makes ネオン工事 a special work only for 自家用電気工作物. A neon distribution board installed in a 一般用電気工作物 falls under Article 3(2), so a second-class electrician may do the work. The reasoning for (4) matches.\",\n      \"Law Article 3(4) and Enforcement Regulation Article 2-3 define 簡易電気工事 as work on 自家用電気工作物 used at 600 V or less, excluding line (電線路) work. An 認定電気工事従事者 may do this work. Grounding work on a 200 V motor falls within that scope, so (5) is correct. The reasoning matches.\",\n      \"The explanation says (3) is the only incorrect option. It gives a specific reason for each option: the answer choice and the four correct statements. There are no calculations, and the cause-and-effect reasoning is consistent.\",\n      \"The problem is text only and has no figure. figureDescription, figureUrls=[] and choiceFigureUrls={} are all consistent.\",\n      \"officialReferenceUrls points to e-Gov versions of the law and enforcement regulation effective 2024-04-01. Every legal claim in the explanation was checked against the attached text of Law Articles 2 and 3 and Enforcement Regulation Articles 2-2 and 2-3. No claims depend on outside sources that were not attached.\",\n      \"The metadata is consistent: exam date 2025-03-23, which is FY2024 (Reiwa 6) lower-half, subject law, problem 2.\"\n    ]\n  }\n]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2694,"cache_read_input_tokens":157019,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2694},"output_tokens":751,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics